[75.172558, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H     06d6278 link-page: mission plan                             \u001b[2;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;114m\r\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[m\u000f(troupe gate plan \"Link page with dark mode: 2 Sonnet      \u001b[4;6H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cbuilders (page, theme) in parallel, Codex reviews.         \r\n      Approve?\" --no-wait)                                       \u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[39mOpened gate plan                                            \u001b[7;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n●\u001b[39m The plan is waiting for your approval in the panel. Here's what\u001b[9;65H\u001b[1K\r  you'd be approving:\u001b[10;65H\u001b[1K\r\n  - \u001b[1mWhat you get:\u001b[m\u000f a static \"My links\" page with a header and four\r\n    links, a light and a dark theme, and a toggle. It follows    \r\n    your system setting the first time, and remembers your choice\u001b[14;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C  after that. The links are read from \u001b[38;5;153mlinks.json\u001b[39m, so changing  \u001b[15;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthem doesn't mean touching the HTML. There's no build step   \u001b[16;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[4G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cand nothing to install.\u001b[17;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- \u001b[1mWho\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mbuilds\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mit:\u001b[m\u000f two builders work at the same time, both on   \u001b[18;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[4G\u001b[1K\u001b[CClaude Sonnet.\u001b[19;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- \u001b[1mpage\u001b[m\u000f does the HTML, the links file and the code that lists \u001b[20;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[6G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthe links.\u001b[21;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- \u001b[1mtheme\u001b[m\u000f does the styles and the dark-mode toggle.            \u001b[22;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[23;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[CA \u001b[1mCodex\u001b[m\u000f reviewer checks each one as it finishes. All three   \u001b[24;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[Crun in their normal ask-first permission mode, not full      \u001b[25;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[4G\u001b[1K\u001b[Caccess.\u001b[26;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[C- \u001b[1mMy\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mrecommendations:\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[27;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- Use placeholder links you replace later.                   \u001b[28;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- Follow the system theme and add the toggle.                \u001b[29;4H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- Serve the page with \u001b[38;5;153mnpm\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;153mstart\u001b[39m, because a browser won't load\u001b[30;6H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthe links from a page opened as a plain file.              \u001b[31;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- \u001b[1mBefore\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mit\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mcounts\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mas\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mdone,\u001b[m\u000f you'll open the page in both themes\u001b[32;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[4G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cand approve how it looks.\u001b[33;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[34;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CPress \u001b[38;5;153ma\u001b[39m in the panel to approve, or \u001b[38;5;153mc\u001b[39m to tell me what to       \u001b[35;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cchange.\u001b[36;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mWorked for 41s · done 7:49 PM\u001b[39m                                  \u001b[38;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n❯ Make it two builders in a chain: a data role for links.json    \r\n  first, then the page with its styles, which waits on data.     \r\n  Cod                                                            \u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[44;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[C⏵⏵\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mbypass\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mpermissions\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mon\u001b[38;5;246m (shift+tab\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mto\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mcycle)\u001b[39m                  \u001b[45;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[34h\u001b[?25h\u001b[42;6H"]
