[292.169993, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[H●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[m\u000f(troupe stage review && troupe dispatch review && troupe   \u001b[2;6H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cwait --role review --ready --timeout 60 && troupe send     \r\n      review \"Review role/link-page/data: links.json wi…)        \u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[38;5;211mError: Exit code 1\u001b[39m                                          \u001b[5;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[5G\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[CStage: review\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;211mDispatched review to %209; /home/tizh/repos/projects/troupe-\u001b[39m\u001b[7;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[Cdemo/.troupe/worktrees/link-page/review on \u001b[39m                 \r\n     \u001b[38;5;211mrole/link-page/review\u001b[39m                                       \u001b[9;65H\u001b[1K\r     \u001b[38;5;211mreview: waits on you\u001b[39m\r\n     \u001b[38;5;211mTrust this folder? Codex can read, edit, and run files here,\u001b[39m\u001b[11;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C   \u001b[38;5;211msubject to your permission settings. Folder settings can \u001b[39m   \u001b[12;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[Crun\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mcode\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mautomatically,\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211meven\u001b[39m                                \u001b[13;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;231m\r\n●\u001b[39m The Codex reviewer has opened, but it's stuck on Codex's \"Trust\r\n  this folder?\" prompt. Please answer it in the \u001b[38;5;153mreview\u001b[39m window in \u001b[16;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthe roles window. I'll send it the data branch to review once  \r\n  it's ready.                                                    \u001b[18;65H\u001b[1K\r\n  The data role finished cleanly. It added \u001b[38;5;153mlinks.json\u001b[39m with the   \u001b[20;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cfour links in order and a test that checks its shape. All tests\u001b[21;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cpass, and it touched only its own files.                       \u001b[22;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;