[1238.269716, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[1;66H│\u001b[2;66H│\u001b[3;66H│\u001b[4;66H│\u001b[5;66H│\u001b[6;66H│\u001b[7;66H│\u001b[8;66H│\u001b[9;66H│\u001b[10;66H│\u001b[11;66H│\u001b[12;66H│\u001b[13;66H│\u001b[14;66H│\u001b[15;66H│\u001b[16;66H│\u001b[17;66H│\u001b[18;66H│\u001b[19;66H│\u001b[20;66H│\u001b[21;66H│\u001b[22;66H│\u001b[23;66H│\u001b[24;66H\u001b[32m│\u001b[25;66H│\u001b[26;66H│\u001b[27;66H│\u001b[28;66H│\u001b[29;66H│\u001b[30;66H│\u001b[31;66H│\u001b[32;66H│\u001b[33;66H│\u001b[34;66H│\u001b[35;66H│\u001b[36;66H│\u001b[37;66H│\u001b[38;66H│\u001b[39;66H│\u001b[40;66H│\u001b[41;66H│\u001b[42;66H│\u001b[43;66H│\u001b[44;66H│\u001b[45;66H│\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[H  troupe won't treat the Codex reviewer window as ready, so the  \u001b[2;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cmessage wasn't sent. It timed out twice, and nothing was typed \u001b[3;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cinto the window.\u001b[4;65H\u001b[1K\r\n  The window does look idle at its prompt. Its status bar shows  \r\n  \"⚠ 3 warnings\", which may be what's keeping troupe from seeing \u001b[7;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cit as ready.                                                   \u001b[8;65H\u001b[1K\n\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[CTwo ways to unblock it:\u001b[10;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[11;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C1. \u001b[1mClear\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mit\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1myourself:\u001b[m\u000f open the \u001b[38;5;153mreview\u001b[39m window and press \u001b[38;5;153mf2\u001b[39m to   \u001b[12;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csee the warnings. Dismiss whatever needs dismissing, then   \u001b[13;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ctell me and I'll send the final review.                     \u001b[14;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C2. \u001b[1mLet\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mme\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mrestart\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mthe\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mreviewer:\u001b[m\u000f I close the review window and  \u001b[15;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Copen a fresh one from the mission branch, which now has both\u001b[16;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Croles merged. You'd likely have to answer Codex's \"Trust    \u001b[17;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[5G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthis folder?\" prompt again.\u001b[18;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[19;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CI'd go with option 1 because it's quicker.                     \u001b[20;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[21;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[COn the page review itself: Codex passed the page branch with no\u001b[22;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cmust-fix findings. It ran the page in a real Chromium browser  \u001b[23;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cand checked:\u001b[24;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the theme is set before the page first draws                 \u001b[25;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the toggle choice survives a reload                          \u001b[26;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- link labels can't inject HTML                                \u001b[27;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the \"couldn't load links\" fallback appears when it should    \u001b[28;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- nothing scrolls sideways at phone width                      \u001b[29;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[30;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CIt left one optional suggestion: the page test checks the link \u001b[31;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cdata rather than the finished list on the page, so it wouldn't \u001b[32;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ccatch someone later swapping in unsafe rendering. The page is  \u001b[33;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csafe as written. I'll list this as an open finding at the MR   \u001b[34;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cgate rather than spend a fix round on it.                      \u001b[35;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mBaked for 3m 27s · done 8:07 PM\u001b[39m                                \u001b[37;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n❯ \u001b[2mCleared the warnings, send the final review\u001b[m\u000f                    \u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\r\n  \u001b[38;5;211m⏵⏵ bypass permissions on\u001b[38;5;246m (shift+tab to cycle) · ← 4 agents\u001b[39m     \u001b[