[1362.657588, "o", "\u001b[1;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C1. \u001b[1mClear\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mit\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1myourself:\u001b[m\u000f open the \u001b[38;5;153mreview\u001b[39m window and press \u001b[38;5;153mf2\u001b[39m to   \u001b[2;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csee the warnings. Dismiss whatever needs dismissing, then   \u001b[3;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ctell me and I'll send the final review.                     \u001b[4;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C2. \u001b[1mLet\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mme\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mrestart\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mthe\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mreviewer:\u001b[m\u000f I close the review window and  \u001b[5;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Copen a fresh one from the mission branch, which now has both\u001b[6;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[Croles merged. You'd likely have to answer Codex's \"Trust    \u001b[7;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[5G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthis folder?\" prompt again.\u001b[8;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[9;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CI'd go with option 1 because it's quicker.                     \u001b[10;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[11;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[COn the page review itself: Codex passed the page branch with no\u001b[12;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cmust-fix findings. It ran the page in a real Chromium browser  \u001b[13;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[2G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cand checked:\u001b[14;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the theme is set before the page first draws                 \u001b[15;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the toggle choice survives a reload                          \u001b[16;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- link labels can't inject HTML                                \u001b[17;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the \"couldn't load links\" fallback appears when it should    \u001b[18;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- nothing scrolls sideways at phone width                      \u001b[19;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[20;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CIt left one optional suggestion: the page test checks the link \u001b[21;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cdata rather than the finished list on the page, so it wouldn't \u001b[22;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Ccatch someone later swapping in unsafe rendering. The page is  \u001b[23;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Csafe as written. I'll list this as an open finding at the MR   \u001b[24;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cgate rather than spend a fix round on it.                      \u001b[25;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mBaked for 3m 27s · done 8:07 PM\u001b[39m                                \u001b[27;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[48;5;237m\r\n❯ \u001b[38;5;231mReview passed the whole branch. Open the MR gate.\u001b[39m              \u001b[49m\u001b[29;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;114m\r\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mBash\u001b[m\u000f(cat /home/tizh/repos/projects/troupe-demo/.troupe/worktree\r\n      s/link-page/review/.troupe/result.md; ls -la               \u001b[32;6H\u001b[1K\u001b[C/home/tizh/repos/projects/troupe-demo/.troupe/worktrees/l…)\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n  ⎿  \u001b[39m---                                                         \u001b[34;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[5G\u001b[1K\u001b[Cstatus: done\r\n     summary: \"PASS mission: integrated tests and browser ch     \u001b[36;5H\u001b[1K\u001b[2m\u001b[C… +21 lines (ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\u000f                              \u001b[37;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;174m\r\n✶\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;174mPolishing… \u001b[38;5;246m(Checking git branch guard… · 5s · ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m545 tokens · \u001b[39m  \u001b[39;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\rthought for 1s)\u001b[39m\u001b[40;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n❯ \u001b[39m                                                               \u001b[38;5;244m\r\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[44;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;211m\u001b[C⏵⏵\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mbypass\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mpermissions\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;211mon\u001b[38;5;246m (shift+tab\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mto\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mcycle)\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246m·\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mesc\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mto\u001b