─────────────────────────────\u001b[17;68H\u001b[39m- The page shows a header and the links from\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;111;168;255mlinks.json\u001b[39m, each opening its target\u001b[18;68H- Editing \u001b[38;2;111;168;255mlinks.json\u001b[39m alone changes the links\u001b[Con the page\u001b[19;68H- The page follows the system light/dark setting on first visit\u001b[20;68H- A toggle switches the theme, and the choice survives a reload\u001b[21;68H- The page works at phone width with no sideways scroll\u001b[22;68H- \u001b[38;2;111;168;255mnpm test\u001b[39m passes, with tests for the link data, the page and the theme logic\u001b[23;68H- You have opened the\u001b[Cpage in both themes and approved how it looks\u001b[25;68H\u001b[38;2;78;105;145m─ \u001b[38;2;232;234;240m\u001b[1mOut of scope\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[38;2;78;105;145m ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[27;68H\u001b[39mReal content beyond placeholders, analytics,\u001b[Ca build step, any framework or npm\u001b[28;68Hdependency, deployment.\u001b[30;68H\u001b[38;2;78;105;145m─ \u001b[38;2;232;234;240m\u001b[1mDecisions for you\u001b[m\u000f\u001b[38;2;78;105;145m ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[32;68H\u001b[39m1. Which links? \u001b[1mRecommended: placeholders\u001b[m\u000f (GitHub, LinkedIn, Blog, Email) with example\u001b[33;71HURLs you replace later, because the mission is about the page, not its content.\u001b[34;68H2. How dark mode works. \u001b[1mRecommended: follow the system setting, plus a toggle whose\u001b[35;71Hchoice is remembered in `localStorage`\u001b[m\u000f, because it does the right thing without a\u001b[36;71Hclick and still lets you override it.\u001b[37;68H3. How the page reads\u001b[C\u001b[38;2;111;168;255mlinks.json\u001b[39m. \u001b[1mRecommended: `links.js` fetches it at load\u001b[m\u000f, served\u001b[38;71Hwith \u001b[38;2;111;168;255mnpm start\u001b[39m (\u001b[38;2;111;168;255mpython3 \u001b[m\u