[1414.091276, "o", "\u001b[H  with how the two parts fit together. All 9 tests pass.         \u001b[2;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[3;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CIf you approve, the MR delivers:                               \u001b[4;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- the \"My links\" page with four placeholder links read from    \u001b[5;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[4G\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;153m\u001b[Clinks.json\u001b[39m\u001b[6;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- a light and a dark theme that follows your system setting    \u001b[7;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- a toggle whose choice is kept after a reload                 \u001b[8;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[C- an \u001b[38;5;153mnpm\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;153mstart\u001b[39m script to serve the page locally                \u001b[9;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[10;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[1m\u001b[COne\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1mopen\u001b[m\u000f \u001b[1msuggestion:\u001b[m\u000f add a test of the finished link list on   \u001b[11;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthe page, not just the link data. My recommendation is to skip \u001b[12;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cit, since the page is safe as written. Say if you want it, and \u001b[13;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cit'll go back to the page role.                                \u001b[14;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[15;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[CI'm counting your \"the page looks good\" as the look approval   \u001b[16;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Cthe plan asks for. Nothing is pushed until you press \u001b[38;5;153ma\u001b[39m to      \u001b[17;2H\u001b[1K\u001b[Capprove; \u001b[38;5;153mc\u001b[39m tells me what to change.                            \u001b[18;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\r\n✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mBrewed for 9s · done 8:11 PM\u001b[39m                                   \u001b[20;65H\u001b[1K\u001b[38;5;246m\u001b[48;5;237m\r\n❯ \u001b[38;5;231mmr-ok approved in the panel. Open the PR, then run troupe \u001b[39m     \r\n  \u001b[38;5;231mstage merged -m link-page and troupe gate merged -m link-page \u001b[39m \r\n  \u001b[38;5;231m\"<the PR link>\". Keep the role windows: the person may ask for\u001b[39m 